  "source_visual_findings": [
    "Original skin weights produce a severe jagged lateral tail fan during brace and hop, around/through the legs. Animation alone cannot repair this.",
    "The existing pilot derivative keeps the selected curl rigidly attached to Pelvis during exit and walk, and all62321 non-tail body vertices match original positions exactly at every sampled frame.",
    "Derivative curl is compact and upright, but conspicuous dangling unselected fur shards persist below the pelvis/behind the knees. It is not a visual pass.",
    "Front/side/rear renders at seven times per configuration show body articulation and foot motion; no actor route, cockpit, deck, camera blending or scale transition is rendered.",
    "Fixed ankle targets in1.6\u20132.4s do not establish sole/deck contact or collision clearance.",
    "Final pose is numerically compatible with A_Walk at0.30833333333333335 seconds; resume that phase or use a deliberate animation blend.",
    "Separate TailCandidate.glb investigation is recorded in ContentSource/TailCandidatePreview/Review.json; existing pilot derivative conclusions above remain unchanged."
